The env_0052_collision_repair_network scenario is finished. All 5 difficulties pass the policy audit and the docs audit, and the final whole-scenario `validate_scenario` check returns `VALID`.

**Blueprint.** The company is Crestline Collision & Glass. The scenario has 8 product categories, 31 database tables and 31 shared lookup tools. The blueprint passed its own checks (BLUEPRINT OK, SHARE TOOLS OK), and the blueprint files were not changed after that.

**Difficulties (2 tasks each)**

| Difficulty | Product | Policy audit | Docs | Docs audit |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| estimate_booking_desk | estimate | PASS (round 2) | 71 | PASS |
| claim_repair_billing_desk | claim | PASS (round 2) | 56 | PASS |
| rental_coordination_desk | rental | PASS (round 3) | 65 | PASS |
| sensor_calibration_desk | adas | PASS (round 2) | 43 | PASS |
| warranty_rework_desk | warranty | PASS (round 2) | 62 | PASS |

- **Unclaimed products:** retail (22 docs), glass (16) and carrier (21) belong to no difficulty. Their docs pass their own render check, but by design they are never audited.
- **Checks:** every instantiate check passes for all five difficulties (re-run by me, not taken from agent reports), and the traceability check passes on the complete docs tree.
- **Cross-difficulty identifiers:** 82 identifiers (phone, email, name, PIN, VIN, insurer claim number), with no duplicates across difficulties.

**What it took**
- **Rework:** every difficulty failed its first policy audit and was reworked:
  - mostly over factor tiers no real customer could ever reach, rules that disagreed with their own calculations, and changes to base rules that weren't declared;
  - task 0 of rental also had a scored day count that no rule determined;
  - warranty's task 0 also had seeded calibration history that broke the calibration desk's own rules.
- **Account cuts:** the run was cut off by account usage limits three times. Each time I checked what was actually on disk:
  - agents with partial work were resumed from their breakpoint;
  - agents that had only read and written nothing (the round-1 warranty instantiation and the first rental render) were restarted fresh.
- **Early start:** I rendered the three unclaimed products, and then claim and estimate, before all difficulties had passed. Nothing still to come could change their inputs.

